# SEO

This is a corporate consulting website.

SEO is an important requirement.

## Metadata

Every important route must have:

- unique title
- unique meta description
- canonical URL where appropriate
- Open Graph metadata

Do not duplicate titles and descriptions across pages.

## Language

Use:

lang="ar"

and RTL.

## Semantic HTML

Prefer:

<header>
<nav>
<main>
<section>
<article>
<footer>

Use headings in a logical hierarchy.

Each page should have one primary H1 unless there is a specific valid reason otherwise.

## Content

Important business content must exist in crawlable HTML.

Do not hide important SEO content behind:
- click-only interactions
- client-only rendering
- unnecessary tabs
- JavaScript-only UI

## URLs

Use clean routes.

Examples:

/about
/services
/services/business-consulting
/services/governance
/why-waei
/clients
/contact

Avoid query-heavy URLs for static pages.

## Sitemap

Generate and maintain:

sitemap.xml

Include public indexable routes.

Do not include:
- admin
- private routes
- duplicate URLs

## Robots

Provide a correct robots.txt.

Do not accidentally block the entire site.

## Structured Data

Use structured data only when it accurately represents the business.

Do not invent:
- ratings
- reviews
- addresses
- social profiles
- business facts

## Images

Images should have meaningful Arabic alt text when informative.

Decorative images should use appropriate empty alt behavior.

## Performance

SEO and performance are connected.

Prioritize:
- fast LCP
- optimized images
- reduced JavaScript
- lazy loading
- minimal third-party scripts

Do not sacrifice accessibility or semantic HTML for superficial Lighthouse scores.